# Dev Notes 54 — Runtime Cancel Action v1

**Date:** 2026-06-20  
**Branch:** `runtime-cancel-action-v1`  
**Status:** Assistant-staged candidate from the preflighted downloaded `main` repo ZIP. Sandbox syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted action-cancellation smoke, execute-action/public-dispatch/nativeWorkerBackend regression smokes, current contract-chain smokes, broader worker/cancellation/lifecycle mock-static smokes, docs propagation review, package extraction/recheck, artifact guard, and Michael local Windows/MINGW64 real-runtime checks passed. GitHub branch verification remains the only incomplete gate before merge readiness.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds a narrow public action-level cancellation surface:

```js
cancelAction(actionId)
```

The implementation intentionally preserves the existing request cancellation path:

```text
cancelAction(actionId)
  -> actionId/requestId registry lookup
  -> existing cancelPrompt(requestId)
  -> existing scheduler/request/worker cancellation path
  -> existing execute-action cancelled outcome mapping
```

This is not a scheduler rewrite, lifecycle rewrite, worker protocol change, or second native cancellation path.

---

## 2. Source basis

The staged candidate was built from the preflighted downloaded repo ZIP copy of GitHub `main` after `runtime-execute-action-public-envelope-dispatch-v1`.

The prior branch established public raw action-envelope dispatch for the built-in route:

```text
text.generate -> nativeWorkerBackend -> native-worker.default
```

That branch left action-level cancellation as future work while preserving request-level cancellation through:

```text
cancelPrompt(requestId)
```

This branch fills that specific control-surface gap.

